<div class="card">
  <h1 class="site-home-h2" style="font-size:2rem">Where we came from.</h1>
  <p class="site-words">I am Philip Ross. I started Quickler in Dundee in March 2026.</p>
  <p class="site-words">I trained as an engineer at Strathclyde and did an internship at an AI analytics start-up. Before Quickler I built small automations for businesses and charities.</p>
  <p class="site-words">The same thing kept showing up. People did the hard part of the job well, on site, then lost hours at the desk typing it up. Muddled notes. Photos to sort. Formatting. The site is where your skill is needed. The desk is not.</p>
  <p class="site-words">So I built Quickler. You talk on WhatsApp as you go round, and send photos when you need to. Quickler puts each thing where it belongs, in your own layout. You read it, change any word, and sign.</p>
  <p class="site-words">It will not be perfect. When you correct it, you teach it, like a new colleague.</p>
  <p class="site-words">If you get stuck, email me at <a href="mailto:philipross@quickler.co">philipross@quickler.co</a>. I read every one.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2 class="site-home-h2">How we work, and why.</h2>
  <p class="site-words">We do not make things up. If you do not say it, it is not in the report. If you do say it, we do not lose it.</p>
  <p class="site-words">You sign, not us. Every word can be changed. Your report keeps your layout, not ours.</p>
  <p class="site-words">No app to install. If it takes training, it gets skipped. So it runs on the WhatsApp already on your phone, or Telegram.</p>
  <p class="site-words">We ship small changes often, and write each one down on <a href="/new/">What's new</a>.</p>
  <p class="site-words">The nine principles are on the <a href="/believe/">principles page</a>.</p>
</div>

